# CkAngelscriptGenerator self-heal stub recovery files (written beside the canonical
# during a failed compile, deleted by OnPostCompile once the canonical regenerates).
Script/Generated/_StubRecovery_*.as
Script/Generated/_StubRecovery_*.json

# Generated EntitySpawnParams - regenerated on every editor boot / AS compile, so tracking it only
# produced merge conflicts and stale commits (a teammate adds a field without regenerating, and
# every other checkout fails to compile). Bootstrap on a fresh clone, or after a pull deletes it,
# is covered by the self-heal dispatcher's source-derived stub synthesis
# (Plugins/CkFoundation/Source/CkAngelscriptGenerator/Claude.md). Same setup as BusterBlock.
# The other generated files (*_AutoTestActors.as, *Assets.as, DynamicHandleTypes.json,
# *_ScriptProcessorDrivers.as) stay committed - the asset registries hard-reference wrapper actor types.
# If CI is ever added: a fresh agent's first cook fails until the self-heal stubs land, so port
# BusterBlock's .runreal/scripts/cook-with-retry.ps1 and its wiring (pipeline-config.ts,
# pipelines/compile.pipeline.ts, buildgraph/Build.xml).
Script/Generated/Mars_EntitySpawnParams.as

# Same for plugin-authored EntitySpawnParams in non-submodule plugins. A committed plugin ESP leaves
# its subclass accessor present, which blocks the self-heal of the base project accessor it subclasses.
# Submodule plugins (CkFoundation, CkTests, ...) carry their own .gitignore.
Plugins/*/Script/Generated/*_EntitySpawnParams.as
Plugins/*/Script/Generated/_StubRecovery_*.as
Plugins/*/Script/Generated/_StubRecovery_*.json
